# control85.rc with ext-pdo dropped, so the pair can be priced against control85
# in the same run rather than across two builds.
#
# THERE IS NO WITH_PDO KNOB. php-wasm hardcodes --enable-pdo into the configure
# line at Makefile:341, alongside --enable-json and --disable-all, so no variable
# turns it off. ${CONFIGURE_FLAGS} is interpolated at the END of that same line
# and ext/pdo/config.m4 declares PHP_ARG_ENABLE([pdo]) with an explicit
# --disable-pdo help string, so appending the negation is the mechanism: autoconf
# takes the last assignment to enable_pdo. The rc is included at Makefile:22 and
# packages/*/static.mak at :244, and packages/sqlite adds its own --enable-pdo for
# WITH_SQLITE=static/shared/dynamic -- WITH_SQLITE=0 below is what keeps that
# branch from landing after this line and winning.
#
# WHAT MAKES IT SAFE. Nothing opens a PDO connection here: pdo_sqlite is not
# compiled in, pdo_pglite and pdo_cfd1 are off, and drupflare/rom talks to
# ctx.storage.sql through a CfwSqlClient. What ext-pdo was still carrying the
# extension for is CLASS CONSTANTS -- core's FetchModeTrait builds
# $fetchModeLiterals out of PDO::FETCH_* as property defaults, so the first
# `new Statement` on a build without the class throws
# Error("Class \"PDO\" not found"). rom/src/pdo-shim.php declares PDO,
# PDOException and PDOStatement in userland with those constants read off a real
# extension, and rom/tests/pdo-shim.php holds the values to it. That shim must be
# in the deployed tree before this variant ships; this rc exists to price it.
#
# THE SIZE IS NOT KNOWN YET. ext/pdo measured 339,704 bytes of BITCODE in the 8.5
# tree, which is not a gzip figure and must never be subtracted from the
# 3,145,728 ceiling -- raw and gzipped have already moved in opposite directions
# here. The gzip delta is whatever inspect-build.sh reports for this variant
# against control85 in the same run.
PHP_VERSION=8.5

MAIN_MODULE=0
ASYNCIFY=0
OPTIMIZE=2
INITIAL_MEMORY=96MB

WITH_VRZNO=1
WITH_LIBXML=static
WITH_DOM=static
WITH_SIMPLEXML=static
WITH_XML=static
WITH_YAML=static
WITH_ZLIB=static

WITH_CTYPE=1
WITH_FILTER=1
WITH_SESSION=1
WITH_TOKENIZER=1

WITH_BCMATH=0
WITH_CALENDAR=0
WITH_EXIF=0

WITH_ICONV=0
WITH_MBSTRING=0
WITH_ONIGURUMA=0
WITH_SQLITE=0
WITH_GD=0
WITH_LIBPNG=0
WITH_LIBJPEG=0
WITH_FREETYPE=0
WITH_LIBWEBP=0
WITH_LIBZIP=0
WITH_PHAR=0
WITH_XMLREADER=0
WITH_XMLWRITER=0
WITH_INTL=0
WITH_TIDY=0
WITH_SDL=0
WITH_OPENSSL=0
WITH_PDO_PGLITE=0
WITH_PDO_CFD1=0
WITH_WAITLINE=0

# opcache is compiled in; file_cache_only is set at runtime from the worker ini
CONFIGURE_FLAGS+= --enable-opcache
# the negation Makefile:341 has no knob for; last --enable/--disable pdo wins
CONFIGURE_FLAGS+= --disable-pdo
